<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khusrau Malik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1160">1160</a>–<a href="/years/1186">1186</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khusrau Malik was the last sultan of the Ghaznavid dynasty, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> over the Ghaznavid lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> from 1160. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> passed to the Ghurids, Mu'izz al-Din Muhammad attacked the Punjab, and in 1186 he took Lahore and captured Khusrau Malik, who was imprisoned and later put to death, ending the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khusrau-malik.jpg" alt="Khusrau Malik" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Billjones94 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Billon_Jital_of_Khusrau_Malik_(Ghaznavid_empire),_struck_in_Lahore.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
